          "path": "_m/u/8/p/9/national-space-facilities-control-and-test-center-wp/yevpatoria-rt-70-radio.jpg",
          "filename": "Radio telescope RT-70.jpg",
          "caption": "Yevpatoria RT-70 radio telescope. Inside an antenna mirror of the radio telescope RT-70. There is a cabin “C” in the center of the main mirror, inside of it on the 1st and 2d floors there are racks of amplifiers on TWT and at the end there are amplifiers on the klystrons which radio broadcast the device “Goliaf”. On the third and fourth floors there are high sensitive cryogenic receiving complexes of 92, 18, 13, 6, 3.5, 1.35cm ranges. There is a counterreflector with four holds above the cabin “C” (the second mirror). The great mirror and the counterreflector are forming double-mirror system of Gregorian and Cassegrain.",
          "alt": "Yevpatoria RT-70 radio telescope. Inside an antenna mirror of the radio telescope RT-70. There is a cabin “C” in the center of the main mirror, inside of it on the 1st and 2d floors there are racks of amplifiers on TWT and at the end there are amplifiers on the klystrons which radio broadcast the device “Goliaf”. On the third and fourth floors there are high sensitive cryogenic receiving complexes of 92, 18, 13, 6, 3.5, 1.35cm ranges. There is a counterreflector with four holds above the cabin “C” (the second mirror). The great mirror and the counterreflector are forming double-mirror system of Gregorian and Cassegrain.",
